    "created_at": "2019-01-23T16:06:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-23T16:06:30Z",
    "body": "This seems to be special to `window.open()`:\r\n```\r\n<iframe name=test></iframe>\r\n<a href=frame.html target=test>a</a>\r\n<a onclick=\"window.open('frame.html', 'test')\">window.open</a>\r\n```\r\nOnly the window.open link will give the frame a non-null `self.opener`. Once it has one, it'll keep it though, so it's stored on the browsing context somehow. And it'll have to be triggered from `window.open()` only somehow.\r\n\r\nThis probably needs to be solved together with https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/313#issuecomment-453648260 to see if \"disowning\" is limited to auxiliary browsing contexts or not.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/456860484/reactions",
